# Colab setup

## 1. Clone the repository and install Python dependencies

```python
import os
import subprocess

REPO_URL = "https://github.com/lluiseriksson/ym-mass-gap-lean-verification.git"
REPO_DIR = "/content/ym-mass-gap-lean-verification"

if not os.path.isdir(REPO_DIR):
    subprocess.run(["git", "clone", REPO_URL, REPO_DIR], check=True)

subprocess.run(["python3", "-m", "pip", "install", "--upgrade", "pip", "-q"], check=True)
subprocess.run(["python3", "-m", "pip", "install", "-r", f"{REPO_DIR}/requirements.txt", "-q"], check=True)
print("Environment ready.")
```

## 2. Install Lean 4

```python
import os
import subprocess

install_cmd = r'''
curl -sSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leanprover/elan/master/elan-init.sh \
| sh -s -- -y --default-toolchain leanprover/lean4:stable
'''
subprocess.run(["bash", "-lc", install_cmd], check=True)
os.environ["PATH"] = os.path.expanduser("~/.elan/bin") + ":" + os.environ["PATH"]
subprocess.run(["bash", "-lc", "source $HOME/.elan/env && lean --version"], check=True)
```

## 3. Build Lean workspace

```bash
%%bash
set -e
source "$HOME/.elan/env"
cd /content/ym-mass-gap-lean-verification/lean
lake update || true
lake exe cache get || true
lake build || true
lake build YMProof || true
```
